HST Office: opening a DOCX does not open the default printer.

Every section of a DOCX import ends in SectionPropertyMap::ApplyPaperSource, which set the page
style's PrinterPaperTray even when the document has no <w:paperSrc> (both trays 0, Word's default
tray). SwXStyle's PaperBin setter first calls getPrinter(true), so every DOCX load created the
document's SfxPrinter for the system default printer: OpenPrinter, DocumentProperties and CreateIC
on that printer while the document loads. Writer's layout does not need it (printer-independent
layout is the default; usePrinterMetrics switches it off separately).

On Windows an unreachable network default printer (WSD/IPP, e.g. a Brother on another subnet) then
blocks the load in the spooler client: winspool.drv shows its own dialog "Waiting for printer
connection... Please wait for printer connection or cancel connection" inside soffice.bin. Found on
test PC HST4 (default printer offline at 192.168.1.207; soffice.bin had WINSPOOL.DRV, PrintConfig.dll,
mxdwdrv.dll and Print.PrintSupport.Source.dll loaded after opening a DOCX). Without <w:paperSrc> the
tray now stays "from printer settings"; documents that name a tray keep the previous behaviour.

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).
Test: open a DOCX without w:paperSrc with an unreachable default printer on Windows: no dialog,
no printer DLLs loaded; a DOCX with w:paperSrc still gets its tray.
---
--- a/sw/source/writerfilter/dmapper/PropertyMap.cxx
+++ b/sw/source/writerfilter/dmapper/PropertyMap.cxx
@@ -621,6 +621,12 @@
